The untrained model exhibits high cross-seed variance and deep-layer collapse, with negative $R^2$ and bimodal behavior across seeds at late layers; this instability indicates that randomly initialized Transformer layers produce destructive interference on action-relevant structure.
The three-condition gradient (trained $>$ Llama-2 base $>$ untrained) holds from L1 through L15, with a reversal at L32 where trained $R^2$ drops below the pretrained baseline.
The qualitative pattern is consistent across all 3 seeds.

