Figure~\ref{fig:action_r2_threecond} compares per-layer action probe $R^2$ across three training stages (untrained, Llama-2 base, VLA-trained) using 50 demonstrations per task, averaged over 3 seeds (mean $\pm$ std).
All three conditions share L0 representations ($R^2 = 0.645 \pm 0.008$); subsequent differences thus arise from Transformer processing rather than input variation.
